WEBVTT

00:00:01.252 --> 00:00:05.464
Ima kara utau koto koko dake no hanashi ni

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:08.926
<i>Shite oite ne</i>

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:14.724
<i>Yokubou wa kokoro ni
kakushite okitai no hontou wa</i>

00:00:14.807 --> 00:00:16.851
<i>Himitsu himitsu</i>

00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:35.703
<i>Chikamichi shitai</i>

00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:39.582
<i>Ame ni nureru koto naku</i>

00:00:39.665 --> 00:00:43.211
Kaze ni tobasareru koto naku

00:00:43.294 --> 00:00:47.006
Zurugashikokute mo waratte ne

00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:51.469
<i>Hikyoumono demo asonde ne</i>

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.056
Kanashimitakunai

00:00:55.139 --> 00:00:58.935
Namida ni nureru koto naku

00:00:59.018 --> 00:01:02.563
<i>Tohou ni kureru koto</i> naku

00:01:02.647 --> 00:01:06.025
Donkan datte waratte ne

00:01:06.108 --> 00:01:11.072
<i>Tanoshii koto dake oshiete ne</i>

00:01:14.825 --> 00:01:19.372
<i>Mitai kao ga aru no kikitai koe ga aru no</i>

00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:24.252
Me <i>ga</i> sametara yorokobi wo narashite

00:01:24.335 --> 00:01:30.299
<i>Ohayou, kyou mo yoroshiku onegai itashimasu</i>

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:31.008
"Princess Jellyfish"

00:01:33.594 --> 00:01:37.223
<i>Mom, it's been three
months since I came to Tokyo.</i>

00:01:37.306 --> 00:01:40.559
<i>I couldn't manage to become a princess,</i>

00:01:40.643 --> 00:01:44.272
<i>but I had</i> a <i>fun life here with the Sisterhood.</i>

00:01:44.355 --> 00:01:48.276
<i>And then, he suddenly appeared before</i> me...

00:01:48.359 --> 00:01:53.531
<i>A very strong, very beautiful, male princess.</i>

00:01:54.407 --> 00:01:56.575
Tsukimi, are you awake?

00:01:57.285 --> 00:02:00.288
"Sukiyaki Western Matsusaka"

00:02:00.371 --> 00:02:02.248
Tsukimi? Is something wrong?

00:02:02.331 --> 00:02:07.336
O-Oh, hello! Sorry, I'm just in
the middle of something right now...

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.588
C-Can I help you?

00:02:09.672 --> 00:02:13.676
I wanted to know if the jellyfish
would be all right left in the bath.

00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:15.219
Who's that?

00:02:15.303 --> 00:02:16.679
Hey-_

00:02:18.014 --> 00:02:19.557
What's the matter, Tsukimi?

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.559
L-I'm fine!

00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:23.477
<i>I-I'll be down soon!</i>

00:02:23.561 --> 00:02:26.355
All right, then, I'll see you downstairs.

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:43.748
My hand... my hand touched a Stylish's mouth!

00:02:43.831 --> 00:02:45.541
And now it's sticky!

00:02:45.624 --> 00:02:48.502
There's weird sticky stuff on me!

00:02:48.586 --> 00:02:49.962
What is it?!

00:02:50.046 --> 00:02:51.422
Lip gloss?

00:02:52.882 --> 00:02:58.346
A-A-A-Anyway, please put
on your clothes and your wig!

00:02:58.429 --> 00:03:00.598
L-I'm begging you---

00:03:00.681 --> 00:03:04.268
You dropped the wig in the hall, though.

00:03:12.818 --> 00:03:14.862
There it is!

00:03:14.945 --> 00:03:17.573
Sheesh, there's nobody here.

00:03:17.656 --> 00:03:20.576
The bathroom's that way, right?
I'll go wash my face and--

00:03:20.659 --> 00:03:22.453
N-N-N-No!

00:03:30.461 --> 00:03:32.171
Tsukimi!

00:03:32.254 --> 00:03:35.424
Emergency! Emergency!

00:03:37.343 --> 00:03:38.302
Whatcha doing?

00:03:38.386 --> 00:03:41.514
The dust was starting to show,
so I'm cleaning everything up!

00:03:41.597 --> 00:03:45.559
Well, come quickly! We have a
desperate situation on our hands!

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:49.688
An applicant?

00:03:49.772 --> 00:03:52.358
Yes, from some self-proclaimed gay men.

00:03:52.441 --> 00:03:53.818
Gay?

00:03:56.737 --> 00:03:59.323
Agents who die in the
field receive no burial!

00:03:59.407 --> 00:04:01.659
Do they think girls like us

00:04:01.742 --> 00:04:04.120
will just squeal for joy at
the thought of a gay couple?

00:04:04.203 --> 00:04:05.955
The fools!

00:04:06.038 --> 00:04:10.167
Gay, transvestite,
or baby--a man is a man!

00:04:10.251 --> 00:04:14.130
No boys may ever enter our holy Nunnery!

00:04:14.213 --> 00:04:15.923
Not even Kong Ming himself!

00:04:16.006 --> 00:04:21.595
I know. I'll send a firm rejection
that leaves no room for appeal.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.893
And... send!

00:04:29.937 --> 00:04:31.147
Who's that?

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:35.609
I thought Banba and Jiji had
both gone to the front lines!

00:04:35.693 --> 00:04:38.237
L-| imagine it's just a cat.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:40.281
A cat? But we don't have one!

00:04:42.783 --> 00:04:44.493
Could it be Ms. Mejiro?!

00:04:44.577 --> 00:04:46.662
She's completely nocturnal.

00:04:46.745 --> 00:04:49.582
She'd never set foot in a sunny hallway.

00:04:49.665 --> 00:04:52.626
She even bought first-rate
light-blocking curtains for the windows.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:56.297
Ah, but her deadline
is coming up, so maybe...

00:04:58.257 --> 00:05:02.845
Ms. Mejiro would never run water so loudly.

00:05:02.928 --> 00:05:03.929
Bandits?!

00:05:04.013 --> 00:05:05.723
We'd better take a look.

00:05:05.806 --> 00:05:07.349
Oh, please, I'll do it!

00:05:07.433 --> 00:05:09.351
This is a job for the building manager.

00:05:09.435 --> 00:05:11.020
Good point...

00:05:13.105 --> 00:05:15.900
Why, there's no one here.

00:05:17.902 --> 00:05:19.862
Were we hearing things?

00:05:21.363 --> 00:05:23.491
Didn't that come from Tsukimi's room?

00:05:23.574 --> 00:05:25.367
<i>L-I'll</i> go look!

00:05:30.247 --> 00:05:32.041
Oh, you're back.

00:05:33.584 --> 00:05:35.753
L-| can't look directly at him!

00:05:38.797 --> 00:05:40.090
Bandits after all?

00:05:40.174 --> 00:05:42.343
N-No, it's no one...

00:05:55.189 --> 00:05:57.399
I-| got it for you.

00:05:57.483 --> 00:06:02.404
This place is cool. Communal
baths, communal washrooms,

00:06:02.488 --> 00:06:05.115
and the layout and
decorating are totally retro!

00:06:05.199 --> 00:06:09.370
It's like chaos. I kinda like it.

00:06:12.206 --> 00:06:14.375
Can I come hang out here again?

00:06:19.755 --> 00:06:21.382
No.

00:06:24.843 --> 00:06:26.345
Okay, see you later!

00:06:26.428 --> 00:06:28.597
I told you, please don't come back!

00:06:33.269 --> 00:06:37.356
<i>Mom, I think this might be
the first time since grade school...</i>

00:06:37.439 --> 00:06:41.777
Yeah. I'm sorry. I spent
all my money on a fish tank...

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:47.616
<i>It's the first time since grade school
I've talked to</i> a <i>man besides my father.</i>

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:52.079
--You take care too, Dad. Bye.
--Even if he is a transvestite.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:03.591
So, how much did this
equipment set you back?

00:07:03.674 --> 00:07:05.968
Well, all together, about 20,000.

00:07:06.051 --> 00:07:11.015
With 20,000, I could get the DVD
box set of Takeo's Dengekil! Strada 5...

00:07:11.098 --> 00:07:13.559
I could get that red agate
sash fastener I saw yesterday...

00:07:13.642 --> 00:07:15.561
"20,000 km Challenge"...

00:07:15.644 --> 00:07:19.523
A whole sixty-volume set of
Records of the <i>Three</i> Kingdoms, used...

00:07:19.607 --> 00:07:23.986
A bold move, Tsukimi!
You're as rash as Zhang Fei!

00:07:25.321 --> 00:07:28.198
So this month is pretty much shot for me.

00:07:28.282 --> 00:07:31.243
Say, who was that female
Stylish from last night?

00:07:31.327 --> 00:07:36.165
Sh-She was just a passerby.
A complete and total stranger!

00:07:36.248 --> 00:07:39.585
But last night she was in the
bathroom watching this jellyfish...

00:07:39.668 --> 00:07:42.755
Really, Tsukimi?

00:07:42.838 --> 00:07:45.591
A-Actually, she was the one
who saved Clara from death

00:07:45.674 --> 00:07:48.844
by forcibly seizing her
from the tropical fish shop!

00:07:48.927 --> 00:07:53.682
She may be one of the Stylish,
but she was quite a skilled fighter!

00:07:53.766 --> 00:07:56.060
Oh ho, well done!

00:07:56.143 --> 00:07:58.979
In Three Kingdoms terms,
I'd say she's Zhou Yu of Wu.

00:07:59.063 --> 00:07:59.980
--Or maybe Zhao Yun of Shu...

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.190
--if we don't stop her fast, she'll make Three Kingdoms
analogies all night. --Or maybe Zhao Yun of Shu...

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:04.652
--if we don't stop her fast, she'll make Three Kingdoms
analogies all night. --No, no, that's probably going too far!

00:08:04.735 --> 00:08:06.195
Yeah...

00:08:06.278 --> 00:08:08.781
Well, today's our hot-pot party day, isn't it?

00:08:08.864 --> 00:08:10.658
It's about time to go shopping.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:13.577
<i>At Amamizu-kan, it's our tradition</i>

00:08:13.661 --> 00:08:16.955
<i>to have a big hot-pot party once a week.</i>

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:19.625
<i>We all decide together
what we'll eat, pool our money,</i>

00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:22.044
<i>and make the meal together.</i>

00:08:22.044 --> 00:08:25.130
"Sukiyaki Sauce"

00:08:26.799 --> 00:08:30.844
What a crime that I never
knew they sold such things!

00:08:30.928 --> 00:08:33.055
It's a "classic cover reprint" of Big-1 gum!

00:08:33.138 --> 00:08:35.849
Here I come!

00:08:35.933 --> 00:08:38.477
It's Kong Ming!

00:08:38.477 --> 00:08:39.436
"Moe Moe Three Kingdoms Gum"

00:08:39.436 --> 00:08:40.688
Die a thousand deaths!

00:08:40.771 --> 00:08:43.732
Mayaya, Banba, it's almost time!

00:08:48.195 --> 00:08:50.614
Red as the flags of Sun (Juan's army!

00:08:50.698 --> 00:08:53.409
Roped with white like
the canals of Guangzhou!

00:08:53.409 --> 00:08:55.994
" M egltiztgyljakilgeef "

00:08:56.078 --> 00:08:57.037
Meat...

00:08:57.121 --> 00:08:58.539
It looks delicious...

00:08:58.622 --> 00:09:00.541
I hope I get to try some one day.

00:09:00.624 --> 00:09:03.085
We can't afford it, so
looking at it will only hurt you.

00:09:03.168 --> 00:09:04.545
Come on, she's here!

00:09:04.628 --> 00:09:08.549
The bearer of half-price stickers
who appears at 6:00 each day!

00:09:08.632 --> 00:09:10.634
Banba, use the Banba Scope.

00:09:10.718 --> 00:09:11.677
Gotcha.

00:09:13.095 --> 00:09:15.514
Clara here. Allow me to explain.

00:09:15.597 --> 00:09:20.769
Banba is able to instinctively
sense which meat is tastiest.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.817
That one... and that one.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.361
Understood. Here we go, Tsukimi!

00:09:29.445 --> 00:09:30.404
coming!

00:09:30.988 --> 00:09:32.072
"Half Price"

00:09:35.993 --> 00:09:38.704
Two hundred grams per person secured!

00:09:38.787 --> 00:09:41.081
Two-thirds of today's meat is pork...

00:09:41.165 --> 00:09:44.126
Look, you. If the cow isn't
tasty, always go with the pig.

00:09:47.171 --> 00:09:49.757
So this place is a vacant lot now too.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:52.426
There are more and
more lately, aren't there?

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:13.363
That's a new model.

00:10:22.331 --> 00:10:24.124
Can I use this?

00:10:25.125 --> 00:10:26.919
Can I come here again?

00:10:38.013 --> 00:10:44.144
"Hypothetically speaking, <i>if</i> someone
were to bring a man into Amamizu-kan...

00:10:44.228 --> 00:10:47.606
I humbly request your decree!

00:10:47.689 --> 00:10:51.318
<i>...what should her punishment be?</i>

00:10:51.401 --> 00:10:53.570
<i>Please give me your opinion."</i>

00:10:57.366 --> 00:10:58.951
"DEATH"

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:01.537
Yes, of course...

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:03.997
Tsukimi, supper is ready!

00:11:09.753 --> 00:11:13.715
Hiya! Is the little jellyfish still alive?

00:11:16.468 --> 00:11:20.639
<i>Mom, your daughter doesn't want to die yet!</i>

00:11:21.557 --> 00:11:22.558
It's commercial time!

00:11:22.641 --> 00:11:24.017
Clara!

00:11:24.977 --> 00:11:26.061
It's the second half!

00:11:26.144 --> 00:11:26.937
Tequila!

00:11:30.566 --> 00:11:35.529
It smells wonderful! Hurry up,
let's put in the other ingredients!

00:11:37.906 --> 00:11:39.700
Come on, come on!

00:11:41.201 --> 00:11:44.371
A word, Tsukimi?

00:11:48.959 --> 00:11:51.670
This is the bright spot of
the Sisterhood's whole week:

00:11:51.753 --> 00:11:53.547
"It's 8:00! Hot-Pot Party!

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:57.050
(Or Grilled Meat or Nagashi
Somen or Whatever in the Summer) "!

00:11:57.134 --> 00:12:01.138
What is that Stylish stranger doing here?!

00:12:01.221 --> 00:12:03.599
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:12:03.682 --> 00:12:06.977
I don't really understand why,
but she came to hang out.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:10.772
I can't just toss her out,
since she saved Clara's life...

00:12:10.856 --> 00:12:14.693
But you didn't have to
give her a place at our feast!

00:12:14.776 --> 00:12:18.238
Everyone's turned to stone.
They can't even hold their chopsticks!

00:12:18.322 --> 00:12:19.698
Clara again!

00:12:19.781 --> 00:12:23.201
Petrification is the Sisterhood's
most powerful self-defensive tool

00:12:23.285 --> 00:12:25.412
here in the desert of Tokyo,

00:12:25.495 --> 00:12:27.789
the concrete jungle crawling
with their natural enemies.

00:12:27.873 --> 00:12:30.208
First, they're automatically petrified

00:12:30.208 --> 00:12:34.296
"First"

00:12:34.296 --> 00:12:35.756
They pretend to be stones on the roadside.

00:12:37.174 --> 00:12:39.801
Second, if the enemy initiates contact,

00:12:39.885 --> 00:12:42.012
they act as if they don't notice.

00:12:42.095 --> 00:12:47.267
This is not "ignoring": they
actually enter a state of non-noticing.

00:12:49.227 --> 00:12:54.024
And third, in the worst case
scenario of an enemy attack,

00:12:54.024 --> 00:12:56.109
"Temporal Lobe"

00:12:56.109 --> 00:12:57.194
they temporarily suspend all
activity in their temporal lobes.

00:12:57.194 --> 00:12:58.362
"Sukiyaki"
"Chii Sanpo" "Kita no Kuni Kara"

00:12:58.362 --> 00:12:59.112
They expunge the incident and
all memories from their brains!

00:12:59.112 --> 00:13:00.906
"Temporal Lobe"

00:13:00.906 --> 00:13:03.867
And after reactivation, they fill in
the blanks with whatever they like!

00:13:03.951 --> 00:13:07.746
I'll try negotiating.
Maybe she'd be willing to go home.

00:13:07.829 --> 00:13:11.041
Please do! Sitting around a
hot-pot with a female Stylish

00:13:11.124 --> 00:13:13.335
is turning our meat into our own poison!

00:13:13.418 --> 00:13:15.712
"Female Stylish"...

00:13:15.796 --> 00:13:18.966
<i>But she's not female!</i>

00:13:23.845 --> 00:13:27.307
Pork is actually pretty good, huh?

00:13:27.391 --> 00:13:29.851
Um... er, you see...

00:13:29.935 --> 00:13:33.230
Hmm, what was your name again?

00:13:33.313 --> 00:13:34.481
Kurashita.

00:13:34.564 --> 00:13:35.524
And your first name?

00:13:35.607 --> 00:13:36.650
Tsukimi.

00:13:36.733 --> 00:13:39.319
Huh, nice name.

00:13:39.403 --> 00:13:42.739
Okay, Tsukimi, honey, let
me serve you up some of this.

00:13:42.823 --> 00:13:45.617
S-So friendly...

00:13:45.701 --> 00:13:47.786
Let's see, is there anything you don't like?

00:13:47.869 --> 00:13:49.788
Can you eat garland chrysanthemums?

00:13:49.871 --> 00:13:52.249
E-Er, I'll eat most things.

00:13:52.332 --> 00:13:57.504
Oh, wow! Sweet herbs sure
don't make this boy want to samba.

00:13:58.463 --> 00:14:00.757
"Boy"?

00:14:00.841 --> 00:14:02.009
Ole'!

00:14:02.092 --> 00:14:08.515
"P Olé, olé! Ba-da-da! Matsuken Samba! <i>P</i>

00:14:08.515 --> 00:14:11.351
--Ah, that song brings back memories!
"P Olé, olé! Ba-da-da! Matsuken Samba! <i>P</i>

00:14:11.435 --> 00:14:14.354
And the Three Kingdoms
puppet theater came on after that!

00:14:14.438 --> 00:14:17.274
<i>And then Walk the Rails of Yesteryear.</i>

00:14:17.357 --> 00:14:18.900
Really?

00:14:18.984 --> 00:14:23.405
That reminds me, didn't you ride
a Metro streetcar recently, Banba?

00:14:23.488 --> 00:14:25.323
I was on my way to the butler café

00:14:25.407 --> 00:14:29.202
when I saw your hair
spilling out of the window...

00:14:30.245 --> 00:14:32.247
Whenever I see those retro
train cars on the Arakawa Line,

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:35.292
I can't help but get on.
It's my pathetic reflex.

00:14:35.375 --> 00:14:38.670
So, who did you go to the butler café with?

00:14:38.754 --> 00:14:42.174
I went alone, would you believe it?

00:14:42.257 --> 00:14:49.514
Retro train cars? Butler cafes?
Wait, is everyone who lives here an otaku?

00:14:49.598 --> 00:14:53.560
<i>...an otaku? Taku? Taku?</i>

00:14:56.146 --> 00:14:58.732
P-Please, I beg you, go home!

00:14:58.815 --> 00:15:01.485
But I came as a girl.

00:15:01.568 --> 00:15:03.445
As long as nobody finds out,
there's no problem, right?

00:15:03.528 --> 00:15:06.114
Then please don't say "boy"!

00:15:06.198 --> 00:15:07.949
Boy, did I really say that?

00:15:08.033 --> 00:15:09.701
You just did it again.

00:15:09.785 --> 00:15:12.204
Why did you come back, anyway?

00:15:12.287 --> 00:15:14.581
Didn't I tell you I would?

00:15:14.664 --> 00:15:17.751
But why did you want to?

00:15:17.834 --> 00:15:23.673
What a silly question.
Because I wanted to see you, Tsukimi!

00:15:23.757 --> 00:15:38.730
<i>Because I wanted to see you, Tsukimi!</i>

00:15:39.356 --> 00:15:42.025
"Because I wanted to see you."

00:15:43.527 --> 00:15:45.112
Talk about delayed reaction...

00:15:48.698 --> 00:15:50.867
She's losing it.

00:15:52.953 --> 00:15:55.205
Isn't this fun?

00:15:55.288 --> 00:15:58.458
Didn't you settle this with her, Tsukimi?

00:15:58.542 --> 00:16:02.379
Mayaya, honey, why
don't you try some meat, too?

00:16:02.462 --> 00:16:04.589
"Mayaya... honey"?!

00:16:04.673 --> 00:16:06.591
Oh, did I get that wrong?

00:16:06.675 --> 00:16:09.594
What gibberish is this Stylish one spouting?

00:16:09.678 --> 00:16:13.306
No one would ever call me
"honey" in the first place! Never!

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:17.853
I could've sworn I heard Tsukimi
here call you that yesterday...

00:16:17.936 --> 00:16:20.230
What about you, Jiji, honey?

00:16:20.313 --> 00:16:22.357
Are you full already?

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:24.734
You do seem like a pretty light eater.

00:16:24.818 --> 00:16:29.030
I don't really care whether
I'm a light eater or not...

00:16:29.156 --> 00:16:30.699
--How utterly rude! In a perfect world, she would pay for
this! --...or more like, it's got nothing to do with this...

00:16:30.699 --> 00:16:32.534
--How utterly rude! In a perfect world, she would pay for this!
--...or more like, I don't want her fussing about stuff like that...

00:16:32.534 --> 00:16:33.493
--How utterly rude! In a perfect world, she would pay for this!
--A lowly Stylish... A lowly Stylish, calling me "honey"!

00:16:33.493 --> 00:16:34.995
--VVeird... --A lowly Stylish... A
lowly Stylish, calling me "honey"!

00:16:34.995 --> 00:16:39.916
“Okay, then, I'll set it here. It won't taste good overcooked.
--A lowly Stylish... A lowly Stylish, calling rne "honey"!

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:41.793
I'm putting in the next batch!

00:16:43.753 --> 00:16:45.630
Hold it.

00:16:45.714 --> 00:16:48.383
Don't put shirataki noodles next to the meat.

00:16:48.466 --> 00:16:50.260
They'll harden it!

00:16:57.142 --> 00:16:58.310
Banba...!

00:17:03.106 --> 00:17:05.108
Me, too.

00:17:05.192 --> 00:17:06.985
You too, Jiji?!

00:17:07.068 --> 00:17:08.236
Wait!

00:17:10.822 --> 00:17:13.200
--Okay, retreat!
--Mayaya?!

00:17:17.537 --> 00:17:20.498
Huh? Why'd they leave?

00:17:22.584 --> 00:17:28.924
I'm sorry, but you could say that
we can't match your enthusiasm...

00:17:29.007 --> 00:17:33.553
If I may put it bluntly,

00:17:33.637 --> 00:17:39.059
no one here particularly
wants to be your friend.

00:17:39.142 --> 00:17:43.521
I say this as daughter
of the building manager:

00:17:43.605 --> 00:17:47.317
please don't come back here again.

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:49.319
Um...

00:17:49.402 --> 00:17:52.572
Sorry I wrecked things.

00:17:54.032 --> 00:17:57.953
I just started having fun...
maybe I got carried away.

00:17:58.036 --> 00:18:00.205
No... um...

00:18:00.288 --> 00:18:02.832
It's like shirataki and meat, I guess...

00:18:02.916 --> 00:18:03.959
Huh?

00:18:04.042 --> 00:18:06.795
When you're near us, we stiffen up, I guess...

00:18:06.878 --> 00:18:08.213
It's chemistry, maybe?

00:18:08.296 --> 00:18:09.881
What are you talking about?

00:18:09.965 --> 00:18:11.299
Nothing...

00:18:11.383 --> 00:18:17.013
See, everybody in my family is busy,
so all of us boys eat separately.

00:18:17.097 --> 00:18:23.895
So I'd never really done stuff like
eat hot-pot meals in a group like that.

00:18:23.979 --> 00:18:26.773
I wanna sizzle! I wanna sizzle!

00:18:26.856 --> 00:18:29.526
You really like that, don't you Tsukimi?

00:18:29.609 --> 00:18:32.821
It's been a long time for me, too, so I have fun.

00:18:32.904 --> 00:18:35.991
Hmm? But you do that all the time, don't you?

00:18:36.074 --> 00:18:39.369
Yes, but that's not what I meant...

00:18:39.452 --> 00:18:44.916
When I was little, my mom and dad
and I ate lots of hot-pot meals, but...

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.460
Where are you from?

00:18:47.544 --> 00:18:49.045
K-Kagoshima.

00:18:49.129 --> 00:18:52.173
Whoa, in Kyushu?! Then you're a Southern girl!

00:18:52.257 --> 00:18:56.386
Yes. But it's cold there in the winter, too,

00:18:56.469 --> 00:19:00.598
so we did lots of hot-pot stuff... but...

00:19:00.682 --> 00:19:04.936
Oh, I get it. Once you move to Tokyo,
you can't visit too often, huh?

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:09.149
What? Oh, no, that's not it...
It's not an issue of Kagoshima being far.

00:19:09.232 --> 00:19:10.984
When I was little, my mother--

00:19:11.067 --> 00:19:14.863
Crap! There's a light on in my old man's room!

00:19:16.239 --> 00:19:19.200
I can't believe he's home at this hour...

00:19:20.493 --> 00:19:24.080
Don't tell me... this is your house?!

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:26.666
Kuranosuke!

00:19:29.419 --> 00:19:34.424
There you go dressing like that again.

00:19:34.507 --> 00:19:36.259
Dad's here today, you know.

00:19:36.259 --> 00:19:40.305
"An adult man wearing a suit!"

00:19:40.305 --> 00:19:42.724
Can you bring me that
Matsusaka beef from yesterday?

00:19:42.807 --> 00:19:44.559
It's still in the fridge, right?

00:19:44.642 --> 00:19:46.686
Excuse me? Why should <i>I</i> go get it?

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:49.147
Oh, I see. If you don't want to,

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:52.192
maybe I'll just visit
Dad's office dressed like this.

00:19:55.028 --> 00:19:56.988
Hide behind the shrubbery!

00:20:03.119 --> 00:20:06.289
To think that the red of
Sun Quan's army now belongs to me!

00:20:08.958 --> 00:20:11.503
The Banba scope is reacting like crazy.

00:20:11.586 --> 00:20:14.047
That proves it's real Matsusaka beef.

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:18.385
Er, does the Sisterhood not have any pride...?

00:20:18.468 --> 00:20:22.305
All right, I'm cooking it up!
Everybody eat all you want!

00:20:22.389 --> 00:20:23.348
Okay!

00:20:24.766 --> 00:20:26.851
This is the most delicious
food in all the kingdoms!

00:20:26.935 --> 00:20:28.436
We'll have to give some to Ms. Mejiro, too.

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:31.731
Um, what about my meat...?

00:20:31.815 --> 00:20:36.778
Clara, he said, "Because
I wanted to see you, Tsukimi."

00:20:38.822 --> 00:20:42.325
In response, the government
held emergency meetings

00:20:42.325 --> 00:20:42.909
"Amamizu-kan"

00:20:42.909 --> 00:20:43.118
--to discuss what should be done
with Diet members Ohno and Matsu.

00:20:43.118 --> 00:20:44.786
"Good morning. --to discuss what should
be done with Diet members Ohno and Matsu.

00:20:44.869 --> 00:20:46.704
--There's Koibuchi again. --However, some in
the Diet say it's too little, too late...

00:20:46.704 --> 00:20:48.248
"Keiichiro Koibuchi, Former Minister of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism" --He's got
a mansion in this neighborhood. --However, sorne in the Diet say it's too little, too late...

00:20:48.248 --> 00:20:49.374
--He's got a mansion in this neighborhood. --However,
some in the Diet say it's too little, too late...

00:20:49.457 --> 00:20:51.418
He does?

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:54.879
"Keiichiro Koibuchi, Former Minister of Land,
Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism"

00:20:55.839 --> 00:20:57.006
Don't tell me...!

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.008
Mom...

00:20:59.092 --> 00:21:01.678
Tsukimi, you're spilling! You're spilling!

00:21:01.803 --> 00:21:04.264
"Koibuchi"

00:21:04.264 --> 00:21:06.683
See you later, big brother!

00:21:06.766 --> 00:21:09.144
You go to school for a change.

00:21:13.064 --> 00:21:18.653
<i>That meat might've been</i> a <i>bribe!</i>

00:21:18.653 --> 00:21:19.988
"Tasty meat."

00:21:21.239 --> 00:21:30.248
<i>Hontou ni kizuite hoshii n da,
anata ga utsukushii tte koto wo</i>

00:21:30.331 --> 00:21:34.669
Ima made naze kizukanai no sa

00:21:34.752 --> 00:21:39.174
<i>Kokoro nakushita mitai da yo</i>

00:21:39.257 --> 00:21:48.349
<i>Sugu ni sugu ni kizuite hoshii, wakatte hoshii yo</i>

00:21:48.433 --> 00:22:02.822
<i>Sugu ni kimi ni kizuite hoshii,
kimi no kirei ni kizuite hoshii yo</i>

00:22:04.199 --> 00:22:08.661
Anata <i>ga</i> totemo kirei dakara

00:22:08.745 --> 00:22:12.749
Anata ni sore wo tsutaetai no sa

00:22:12.832 --> 00:22:22.425
<i>ltsumademo, itsumademo kimi utsukushisa wo</i>

00:22:22.509 --> 00:22:30.850
Anata <i>ga</i> jibun no utsukushisa ni
kizuitara boku <i>wa</i> shiawase nan da

00:22:30.934 --> 00:22:35.647
<i>Boku wa kimi wo omotteru yo</i>

00:22:35.730 --> 00:22:44.989
<i>Kimi no kirei ni kizuite okure</i>
